5. Lower the bar down to the position de départ.
6. Alternate in this manner until you complete the recommended amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Bradford_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Cable Chest Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. Position dual pulleys to poitrine height and select an appropriate poids. Stand a foot or two in front of the cables, holding one in each hand. You can stagger your stance for better stability.
2. Position the upper arm at a angle de 90 degrés with the omoplates together. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the rest of the body stationary, extend through the coudes to press the handles forward, drawing them together in front of you.
4. Pause at the top of the motion, and Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Cable_Chest_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Cable Lift', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle on a tower, and move the cable to the lowest pulley position.
2. With your side to the cable, grab the handle with one hand and step away from the tower. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the poids on the cable. Your outstretched arm should be aligned with the cable.
3. With vos pieds positioned épaule width apart, squat down and grab the handle with both hands. vos bras should still be fully extended.
4. In one motion, pull the handle up and across votre corps until vos bras are in a fully-extended position above votre tête.
5. Keep votre dos straight and vos bras close to votre corps as you pivot votre dos foot and straighten vos jambes to get a full range of motion.
6. Retract vos bras and then votre corps. Return to the neutral position in a slow and controlled manner.
7. Répétez to failure.
8. Then, reposition and Répétez the same series of movements on the opposite side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Cable_Lift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Cable Wood Chop', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle to a tower, and move the cable to the highest pulley position.
2. With your side to the cable, grab the handle with one hand and step away from the tower. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the poids on the cable. Your outstretched arm should be aligned with the cable.
3. With vos pieds positioned épaule width apart, reach upward with your other hand and grab the handle with both hands. vos bras should still be fully extended.
4. In one motion, pull the handle down and across votre corps to your front genou while rotating your torse.
5. Keep votre dos and arms straight and sangle abdominale tight while you pivot votre dos foot and bend your genous to get a full range of motion.
6. Maintain your stance and straight arms. Return to the neutral position in a slow and controlled manner.
7. Répétez to failure.
8. Then, reposition and Répétez the same series of movements on the opposite side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Cable_Wood_Chop/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Calf Raises', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the padded lever of the calf raise machine to fit your height.
2. Place your épaules under the pads provided and position your toes facing forward (or using any of the two other positions described at the beginning of the chapter). The balls of vos pieds should be secured on top of the calf block with the heels extending off it. Push the lever up by extending your hanches and genous until your torse is standing erect. The genous should be kept with a slight bend; never locked. Toes should be facing forward, outwards or inwards as described at the beginning of the chapter. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Raise your heels as you Expirez by extending your chevilles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genou is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down.
4. Go back Lentement, to the position de départ as you Inspirez by lowering your heels as you bend the chevilles until mollets are stretched.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Calf_Raises/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Concentration Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Taking a haltère in your working hand, lean forward. Allow your working arm to hang perpendiculaire à the ground with the coude pointing out. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Flex the coude to curl the poids, keeping the upper arm stationary. At the top of the repetition, flex the biceps and pause.
3. Lower the haltère back to the position de départ.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Concentration_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright holding two haltères in vos mains by your sides. Place the ball of the foot on a sturdy and stable wooden board (that is around 2-3 inches tall) while your heels extend off and touch le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
2. With the toes pointing either straight (to hit all parts equally), inwards (for emphasis on the outer head) or outwards (for emphasis on the inner head), raise the heels off le sol as you expirez by contracting the mollets. Hold the top contraction for a second.
3. As you inspirez, go back to the position de départ by Lentement, lowering the heels.
4. Répétez for the recommended amount of times.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Standing with vos pieds épaule width apart, take a haltère in each hand. Raise the haltères to head height, the coudes out and about 90 degrees. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Maintaining strict technique with no leg drive or leaning back, extend through the coude to raise the poids together directly above votre tête.
3. Pause, and Lentement, return the poids to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Reverse Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec a haltère in each hand using a pronated grip (paumes vers down). vos bras should be fully extended while vos pieds are épaule width apart from each other. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the muscle.
3. Lentement, begin to bring the haltères back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Reverse_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Straight-Arm Front Delt Raise Above Head', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Hold the haltères in front of your cuisses, paumes vers your cuisses.
2. Keep vos bras straight with a slight bend at the coudes but keep them locked. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Raise the haltères in a semicircular motion to arm''s length overhead as you expirez.
4. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ using the same path as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Straight-Arm_Front_Delt_Raise_Above_Head/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec a haltère held by both hands. vos pieds should be about épaule width apart from each other. Lentement, use both hands to grab the haltère and lift it over votre tête until both arms are fully extended.
2. The resistance should be resting in the palms of vos mains with your thumbs around it. The palm of the hands should be facing up towards the ceiling. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping your upper arms close to votre tête with coudes in and perpendiculaire à le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind votre tête until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step.
4. Go back to the position de départ by using the triceps to raise the haltère. Expirez as you perform this step.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Upright Row', 'Trapèzes', 'Haltères', '1. Grasp a haltère in each hand with a pronated (palms forward) grip that is slightly less than épaule width. The haltères should be resting on top of your cuisses. vos bras should be extended with a slight bend at the coudes and votre dos should be straight. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Use your side épaules to lift the haltères as you expirez. The haltères should be close to the body as you move it up and the coudes should drive the motion. Continue to lift them until they nearly touch your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the haltères, your coudes should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement.
3. Lower the haltères back down Lentement, to the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Upright_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Elevated Quad Stretch', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Start by standing with votre dos about two to three feet away from a banc or step.
2. Lift one leg behind you and rest your foot on the step,either on your instep or the ball of your foot, whichever you find most comfortable.
3. Keep your supporting genou slightly bent and avoid letting that genou extend out beyond your toes. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Elevated_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Front Barbell Raise Over Head', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec a barre in vos mains. You should grip the bar with paumes vers down and a closer than épaule width grip apart from each other.
2. vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other. Your coudes should be slightly bent. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lift the barre up until it is directly over votre tête while exhaling. Make sure to keep your coudes slightly bent when performing each repetition.
4. Once you feel the contraction, begin to lower the barre back down to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Front_Barbell_Raise_Over_Head/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Gastrocnemius Calf Stretch', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. Place your right heel on a step with your genou extended and lean forward to grab your right toe with your right hand. Your left genou should be slightly bent and votre dos should be straight.
2. Support your poids on your left leg and place your left hand on your left cuisse.
3. Pull your right toes toward your genou until you feel a stretch in your calf.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Gastrocnemius_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Hamstring and Calf Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Being by looping a belt, band, or rope around one foot. While standing, place that foot forward.
2. Bend votre dos leg, while keeping the front one straight. Now raise the toes of your front foot off of the ground and lean forward.
3. Using the belt, pull on the top of the foot to increase the stretch in the calf. Maintenez 10-20 secondes and Répétez with the other foot.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Hamstring_and_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Hip Circles', 'Abducteurs', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin standing on one leg, holding to a vertical support.
2. Raise the unsupported genou to 90 degrees. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Open the hanche as far as possible, attempting to make a big circle with your genou.
4. Perform this movement Lentement, for a number of repetitions, and Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Hip_Circles/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Hip Flexors', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec the spine vertical, the left foot slightly in front of the right.
2. Bend both genous and lift the back heel off le sol as you press the right hanche forward. You can''t get a thorough, deep stretch in this position, however, because it''s hard to relax the hanche flexor and stand on it at the same time. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Hip_Flexors/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Inner-Biceps Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec a haltère in each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse. vos jambes should be at about épaule''s width apart from each other.
2. Rotate the palms of the hands so that they are facing inward in a neutral position. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids out while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Your poignet should turn so that when the poids are fully elevated you have supinated grip (paumes vers up).
4. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Conseil : Keep the forearms aligned with your outer deltoids.
5. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps.
6. Lentement, begin to bring the haltères back to the position de départ as your Inspirez. Remember to rotate the poignets as you lower the poids in order to switch back to a neutral grip.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Inner-Biceps_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Lateral Stretch', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Take a slightly wider than hanche distance stance with your genous slightly bent.
2. Place your right hand on your right hanche to support the spine.
3. Raise your left arm in a vertical line and place your left hand behind votre tête. Keep it there as you incline your torse to the right.
4. Keep your poids evenly distributed between both legs (don''t lean into your left hanche). Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Lateral_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Leg Curl', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the machine lever to fit your height and lie with your torse bent at the waist facing forward around 30-45 degrees (since an angled position is more favorable for ischio-jambiers recruitment) with the pad of the lever on the back of your right leg (just a few inches under the mollets) and the front of the right leg on top of the machine pad.
2. Keeping the torse bent forward, ensure your leg is fully stretched and grab the side handles of the machine. Position your toes straight. C''est votre position de départ.
3. As you expirez, curl your right leg up as far as possible without lifting the upper leg from the pad. Once you hit the entièrement contracté position, hold it for a second.
4. As you inspirez, bring the legs back to the initial position. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
5. Perform the same exercise now for the left leg.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Leg_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Long Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. This drill is best done in sand or other soft landing surface. Ensure that you are able to measure distance. Stand in a partial squat stance with feet épaule width apart.
2. Utilizing a big arm swing and a countermovement of the legs, jump forward as far as you can.
3. Attempt to land with vos pieds out in front you, reaching as far as possible with vos jambes.
4. Measure the distance from your landing point to the starting point and track results.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Long_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Low-Pulley Deltoid Raise', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Start by standing to the right side of a low pulley row. Use your left hand to come across the body and grab a single handle attached to the low pulley with a pronated grip (paumes vers down). Rest your arm in front of you. Your right hand should grab the machine for better support and balance.
2. Make sure that votre dos is erect and vos pieds are épaule width apart from each other. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin to use the left hand and come across votre corps out until it is elevated to épaule height while exhaling.
4. Feel the contraction at the top for a second and begin to Lentement, lower the handle back down to the original position de départ while inhaling.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
6. Switch arms and Répétez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Low-Pulley_Deltoid_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Low-Pulley One-Arm Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Grab a single handle with your left arm next to the low pulley machine. Turn away from the machine keeping the handle to the side of votre corps with your arm fully extended. Now use both hands to elevate the single handle directly above the head with the paumes vers l''avant. Keep your upper arm completely vertical (perpendiculaire à le sol) and put your right hand on your left coude to help keep it steady. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping your upper arms close to votre tête (coudes in) and perpendiculaire à le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind votre tête until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step.
3. Go back to the position de départ by using the triceps to raise the single handle. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
5. Switch arms and Répétez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Low-Pulley_One-Arm_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Military Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Start by placing a barre that is about poitrine high on a squat rack. Once you have selected the poids, grab the barre using a pronated (paumes vers l''avant) grip. Make sure to grip the bar wider than épaule width apart from each other.
2. Slightly bend the genous and place the barre on your collar bone. Lift the barre up keeping it lying on your poitrine. Take a step back and position vos pieds épaule width apart from each other.
3. Once you pick up the barre with the correct grip length, lift the bar up over votre tête by locking vos bras. Hold at about épaule level and slightly in front of votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lower the bar down to the collarbone Lentement, as you inspirez.
5. Lift the bar back up to the position de départ as you expirez.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Military_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Olympic Plate Hand Squeeze', 'Avant-bras', 'Autre', '1. To begin, stand straight while holding a poids plate by the ridge at arm''s length in each hand using a neutral grip (paumes vers in). You feet should be épaule width apart from each other. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lower the plates until the fingers are nearly extended but can still hold poids. Inspirez as you lower the plates.
3. Now raise the plates back to the position de départ as you expirez by closing vos mains.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. prescribed in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Olympic_Plate_Hand_Squeeze/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing One-Arm Cable Curl', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. Start out by grabbing single handle next to the low pulley machine. Make sure you are far enough from the machine so that your arm is supporting the poids.
2. Make sure that your upper arm is stationary, perpendiculaire à le sol with coudes in and paumes vers l''avant. Your non lifting arm should be grabbing your waist. This will allow you to keep your balance.
3. Lentement, begin to curl the single handle upwards while keeping the upper arm stationary until your forearm touches your biceps while exhaling. Conseil : Only the forearm should move.
4. Hold the contraction position as you squeeze the biceps and then lower the single handle back down to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
6. Switch arms while performing cet exercice.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_One-Arm_Cable_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing One-Arm Dumbbell Curl Over Incline Bench', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Stand on the back side of an incline banc as if you were going to be a spotter for someone. Have a haltère in one hand and rest it across the incline banc with a supinated (palms up) grip.
2. Position your non lifting hand at the corner or side of the incline banc. The poitrine should be pressed against the top part of the incline and vos pieds should be pressed against le sol at a wide stance. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the haltère upward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltère is at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde.
4. Lentement, begin to bring the haltères back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
6. Switch arms while performing cet exercice.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Curl_Over_Incline_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec a haltère held in one hand. vos pieds should be about épaule width apart from each other. Now fully extend the arm with the haltère over votre tête. Conseil : The small finger of your hand should be facing the ceiling and the palm of your hand should be facing forward. The haltère should be above votre tête.
2. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping your upper arm close to votre tête (coudes in) and perpendiculaire à le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind votre tête until your forearm touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arm should remain stationary and only the forearm should move. Inspirez as you perform this step.
4. Go back to the position de départ by using the triceps to raise the haltère. Expirez as you perform this step.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
6. Switch arms and Répétez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Overhead Barbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. To begin, Levez-vous holding a barre or e-z bar using a pronated grip (paumes vers l''avant) with vos mains closer than épaule width apart from each other. vos pieds should be about épaule width apart.
2. Now elevate the barre above votre tête until vos bras are fully extended. Keep your coudes in. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping your upper arms close to votre tête and coudes in, perpendiculaire à le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind votre tête until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step.
4. Go back to the position de départ by using the triceps to raise the barre. Expirez as you perform this step.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Overhead_Barbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Palm-In One-Arm Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Start by having a haltère in one hand with your arm fully extended to the side using a neutral grip. Use your other arm to hold on to an incline banc to keep your balance.
2. vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other. Now Lentement, lift the haltère up until you create a angle de 90 degrés with your arm. Note: Your forearm should be perpendiculaire à le sol. Continue to maintain a neutral grip throughout the entire exercise.
3. Lentement, lift the haltère up until your arm is fully extended. This the position de départ.
4. While inhaling lower the poids down until your arm is at a angle de 90 degrés again.
5. Feel the contraction for a second and then lift the poids back up towards the position de départ while exhaling. Remember to hold on to the incline banc and keep vos pieds positioned to keep balance during the exercise.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
7. Switch arms and Répétez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Palm-In_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Palms-In Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Start by having a haltère in each hand with your arm fully extended to the side using a neutral grip. vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other. Now Lentement, lift the haltères up until you create a angle de 90 degrés with vos bras. Note: Your forearms should be perpendiculaire à le sol. This the position de départ.
2. Continue to maintain a neutral grip throughout the entire exercise. Lentement, lift the haltères up until vos bras are fully extended.
3. While inhaling lower the poids down until your arm is at a angle de 90 degrés again.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Palms-In_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Palms-Up Barbell Behind The Back Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Start by standing straight and holding a barre behind your fessiers at arm''s length while using a pronated grip (palms will be facing back away from the fessiers) and having vos mains épaule width apart from each other.
2. You should be looking straight forward while vos pieds are épaule width apart from each other. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While exhaling, Lentement, elevate the barre up by curling your poignet in a semi-circular motion towards the ceiling. Note: Your poignet should be the only body part moving for cet exercice.
4. Hold the contraction for a second and lower the barre back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
6. When finished, lower the barre down to the squat rack or le sol by bending the genous. Conseil : It is easiest to either pick it up from a squat rack or have a partner hand it to you.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Palms-Up_Barbell_Behind_The_Back_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Pelvic Tilt', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Start off with vos pieds hanche-distance apart.
2. Bend your genous slightly to keep them soft and springy.
3. You may want to move your pelvis forward and backward and back few times before holding the tailbone forward in this stretch.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Pelvic_Tilt/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Rope Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope to a high pulley and select an appropriate poids.
2. Tenez-vous debout avec votre dos to the cable tower. Take the rope with both hands over your épaules, holding it to your upper poitrine. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Perform le mouvement by flexing the spine, crunching the poids down as far as you can.
4. Hold the peak contraction for a moment before returning to the position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Rope_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Soleus And Achilles Stretch', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds hanche-distance apart, one foot slightly in front of the other.
2. Bend both genous, keeping votre dos heel on le sol. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Soleus_And_Achilles_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Toe Touches', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec some space in front and behind you.
2. Bend at the waist, keeping vos jambes straight, until you can relax and let your upper body hang down in front of you. Let vos bras and hands hang down naturally. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Toe_Touches/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Towel Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec both arms fully extended above the head holding one end of a towel with both hands. Your coudes should be in and the arms perpendiculaire à le sol with the paumes vers each other while vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Now communicate with your partner so that he/she can grip the other side of the towel to apply resistance. Keeping your upper arms close to votre tête (coudes in) and perpendiculaire à le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind votre tête until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step.
3. Go back to the position de départ by using the triceps to raise the towel. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Towel_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Two-Arm Overhead Throw', 'Épaules', 'Medecine ball', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds épaule width apart holding a medicine ball in both hands. To begin, reach the medicine ball deep behind votre tête as you bend the genous slightly and lean back.
2. Violently throw the ball forward, flexing at the hanche and using your whole body to complete le mouvement.
3. The medicine ball can be thrown to a partner or to a wall, receiving it as it bounces back.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Two-Arm_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Star Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin in a relaxed stance with vos pieds épaule width apart and hold vos bras close to the body.
2. To initiate the move, squat down halfway and explode back up as high as possible. Fully extend your entire body, spreading vos jambes and arms away from the body.
3. As you land, bring your limbs back in and absorb your impact through the legs.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Star_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Step-up with Knee Raise', 'Fessiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand facing a box or banc of an appropriate height with vos pieds together. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin le mouvement by stepping up, putting your left foot on the top of the banc. Extend through the hanche and genou of your front leg to Levez-vous on the box. As you stand on the box with your left leg, flex your right genou and hanche, bringing your genou as high as you can.
3. Reverse this motion to step down off the box, and then Répétez the sequence on the opposite leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Step-up_with_Knee_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Step Mill', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the stepmill and select the desired option from the menu. You can choose a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Use caution so that you don''t trip as you climb the stairs. It is recommended that you maintain your grip on the handles so that you don''t fall.
2. Stepmills offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than running outside while offering a similar rate of calories burned. They are typically much harder than other cardio equipment. A 150 lb person will typically burn over 300 calories in 30 minutes, compared to about 175 calories walking.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Step_Mill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stiff-Legged Barbell Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Grasp a bar using an prise en pronation (paumes vers down). You may need some poignet wraps if using a significant amount of poids.
2. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse straight and vos jambes spaced using a épaule width or narrower stance. The genous should be slightly bent. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the genous stationary, lower the barre to over the top of vos pieds by bending at the hanches while keeping votre dos straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from le sol until you feel a stretch on the ischio-jambiers. Inspirez as you perform this movement.
4. Start bringing your torse up straight again by extending your hanches until you are back at the position de départ. Expirez as you perform this movement.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stiff-Legged_Barbell_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stiff-Legged Dumbbell Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Haltères', '1. Grasp a couple of haltères holding them by your side at arm''s length.
2. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse straight and vos jambes spaced using a épaule width or narrower stance. The genous should be slightly bent. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the genous stationary, lower the haltères to over the top of vos pieds by bending at the waist while keeping votre dos straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from le sol until you feel a stretch on the ischio-jambiers. Expirez as you perform this movement
4. Start bringing your torse up straight again by extending your hanches and waist until you are back at the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this movement.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stiff-Legged_Dumbbell_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stiff Leg Barbell Good Morning', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Keeping vos jambes stationary, move your torse forward by bending at the hanches while inhaling. Lower your torse until it is parallel with le sol.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by elevating your torse back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stiff_Leg_Barbell_Good_Morning/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stomach Vacuum', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds épaule width apart from each other. Place vos mains on your hanches. C''est votre position de départ.
